course: dictionary
lesson: 4702
title: Honeycreepers and their beaks
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A honeycreeper is a small bird, often brightly coloured, that feeds on nectar and insects. Nectar is the sweet liquid inside flowers. Honeycreepers live in Hawaii and in tropical America.
explain: The example says «Hawaiian honeycreepers all came from one kind of finch and now have many beak shapes, like curved beaks for sipping nectar». The clue is the beak: a bird's beak is shaped for the food it eats. A curved beak helps a honeycreeper sip nectar from flowers.
explain: Scientists call this adaptive radiation: one ancestor gives rise to many kinds, each with a beak for a different food. Darwin's finches are a famous example of the same idea. Many honeycreepers are now endangered, which means they are at risk of dying out.
fact: A honeycreeper is a small, often brightly coloured bird that feeds on nectar and insects.
fact: Nectar is the sweet liquid found inside flowers.
fact: Hawaiian honeycreepers came from one kind of finch, but now they have many beak shapes.
fact: Many Hawaiian honeycreepers are endangered because mosquitoes spread bird malaria and their forest homes were lost.
fact: In Central and South America, the red-legged honeycreeper is bright blue.
exercise: What does a honeycreeper eat? | Grass and leaves | Fish from rivers | *Nectar and insects
exercise: «...curved beaks for sipping nectar» What is a curved beak used for here? | *Sipping nectar from flowers | Digging holes in the ground | Catching fish in the sea
exercise: Many honeycreepers are endangered. What does endangered mean? | Brightly coloured | *At risk of dying out | Very loud
test: What does a honeycreeper's beak shape depend on? | Its name | Its age | Its colour | *Its food
test: Which honeycreeper is bright blue? | A finch from the desert | A penguin from the south | A Hawaiian mosquito | *The red-legged honeycreeper
exam: Which sentence uses honeycreeper correctly? | Honeycreeper means a very loud noise | Honeycreepers are a kind of tree that grows in deserts | *A small, bright bird sipped nectar from the flower | A honeycreeper is a large fish that swims in the sea
